      "content": "\"It is abundantly clear to us that the Indian populace, while possessing certain ancient customs, lacks the modern administrative rigor necessary for true progress. Our stewardship is not an imposition, but rather a solemn obligation to guide this vast subcontinent toward enlightened governance and industrial order. By instilling the principles of structured law and rational infrastructure, we merely provide the necessary framework for their own, albeit dormant, advancement. To withdraw now would be an abdication of duty to a people incapable of administering their own prosperity.\"",
